 '[{"text":"CN VII","isCorrect":false},{"text":"CN X","isCorrect":true},{"text":"CN XII","isCorrect":false},{"text":"CN IX","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'The vagus nerve is the tenth cranial nerve (CN X), with extensive parasympathetic distribution to the thorax and abdomen.'),
('NEET PG', 'Pre- and Para-Clinical Sciences', 'Anatomy', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'The diaphragm is primarily innervated by which nerve?',
 '[{"text":"Vagus nerve","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Phrenic nerve","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Intercostal nerves alone","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Sciatic nerve","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'The phrenic nerve (arising mainly from C4, with contributions from C3 and C5) provides the primary motor innervation to the diaphragm.'),
('NEET PG', 'Pre- and Para-Clinical Sciences', 'Anatomy', 'hard', 'mcq',
 'The hepatic portal vein is formed by the union of which two veins?',
 '[{"text":"Renal vein and hepatic vein","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Superior mesenteric vein and splenic vein","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Inferior vena cava and superior vena cava","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Gastric vein and renal vein","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'The hepatic portal vein is formed behind the neck of the pancreas by the union of the superior mesenteric vein and the splenic vein.'),

